54-79: streamFileLines collects all lines; prefer an async iterator or drop this helper
Collecting into lines: string[] defeats streaming’s memory benefits. Two better options:

Expose an async iterator (e.g., async function* iterateFileLines(filePath) and yield trimmed lines), or
Remove this helper and push callers to processFileLines.

Example iterator sketch (outside this range):
export async function* iterateFileLines(filePath: string): AsyncGenerator<string> {
  const rl = createInterface({ input: createReadStream(filePath, { encoding: "utf-8" }), crlfDelay: Infinity });
  for await (const raw of rl) {
    const trimmed = raw.trim();
    if (trimmed.length > 0) yield trimmed;
  }
}


